<a name="zend.mail.html-mails"></a>45.5. HTML E-Mail</h2></div></div></div>
<p>
        To send an e-mail in <acronym class="acronym">HTML</acronym> format, set the body using the method
        <code class="methodname">setBodyHTML()</code> instead of <code class="methodname">setBodyText()</code>.
        The <acronym class="acronym">MIME</acronym> content type will automatically be set to
        <span class="property">text/html</span> then. If you use both <acronym class="acronym">HTML</acronym> and Text
        bodies, a multipart/alternative <acronym class="acronym">MIME</acronym> message will automatically be
        generated:
    </p>
<div class="example">
<a name="zend.mail.html-mails.example-1"></a><p class="title"><b>Example 45.7. Sending HTML E-Mail</b></p>
<div class="example-contents"><pre class="programlisting">
$mail = new Zend_Mail();
$mail-&gt;setBodyText('My Nice Test Text');
$mail-&gt;setBodyHtml('My Nice &lt;b&gt;Test&lt;/b&gt; Text');
$mail-&gt;setFrom('somebody@example.com', 'Some Sender');
$mail-&gt;addTo('somebody_else@example.com', 'Some Recipient');
$mail-&gt;setSubject('TestSubject');
$mail-&gt;send();
</pre></div>
</div>
<br class="example-break">
</div>
